            <div class="card-body">
                <div>
    <h2>News</h2>
    <h3 class="card-title dpma-card-min"><a href="https://register.dpma.de/DPMAregister/service/aktuelles#a79">Selection guide for Locarno classes</a>
    <span class="dpma-datum"> (29.10.2025)</span></h3>
    <!-- <h2 class="dpma-h_link" id="a81">Selection guide for Locarno classes<span class="dpma-datum"> (29.10.2025)</span></h2> -->
    <p class="mehrzeilig-ellipsis">
        A new selection tool is available for the Locarno classes in the search interfaces for designs
        (Basic, Expert, Advanced, Monitoring, DDDesigns Basic, DDDesigns Expert). If you click on the
        magnifying glass button in the ?Class(es)? field, a drop-down menu opens with a list of the 32 main
        classes of the Locarno classification. By clicking on the plus sign, you can display the individual
        subclasses.<br>Alternatively, enter your desired search term in the ?Filter by search term? search
        field and it will be highlighted. As soon as you click on a search term/menu item, the class number
        is added to the ?Class(es)? input field. With a preceding space if there are already numbers in the
        input field. You can still enter a Locarno class number in the ?Class(es)? field without using the
        input help.
    </p>
    <hr>

    <h3 class="card-title dpma-card-min"><a href="https://register.dpma.de/DPMAregister/service/aktuelles#a78">Convenient entry of image classes</a>
    <span class="dpma-datum"> (18.07.2025)</span></h3>
    <!-- <h2 class="dpma-h_link" id="a80">Convenient entry of image classes<span class="dpma-datum"> (18.07.2025)</span></h2> -->
    <p class="mehrzeilig-ellipsis">
        As soon as you have logged in, you can save your search favourites from the expert search history. A
        search term from the favourites list is inserted into the expert search input field using the search
        favourites selection list.
    </p>
    <hr>

    <h3 class="card-title dpma-card-min"><a href="https://register.dpma.de/DPMAregister/service/aktuelles#a77">Convenient entry of Nice classes also in the extended search</a>
    <span class="dpma-datum"> (18.07.2025)</span></h3>
    <!-- <h2 class="dpma-h_link" id="a78">Convenient entry of image classes<span class="dpma-datum"> (18.07.2025)</span></h2> -->
    <p class="mehrzeilig-ellipsis">
        The new selection aid for Nice classes for trade marks was previously available in the basic search,
        in monitoring and in the screen for defining courier monitoring. The selection aid is now also
        available in the extended search.
    </p>
    <hr>

    <h3 class="card-title dpma-card-min"><a href="https://register.dpma.de/DPMAregister/service/aktuelles#a75">New function for sending e-mails from 
    <span class="baustein_farbe">DPMA</span><span class="baustein_weight">kurier</span></a>
    <span class="dpma-datum"> (15.04.2025)</span></h3>
    <p class="mehrzeilig-ellipsis">
        We have revised the e-mail dispatch of <span class="baustein_farbe">DPMA</span><span class="baustein_weight">kurier</span>. As before, you have the choice between two options.
        You can either choose to be informed about all monitoring, regardless of whether there is news or
        not. You will then receive a daily or weekly e-mail, depending on the delivery frequency. Or, if the
        inbox should rather contain less mail, the second option helps, where
        <span class="baustein_farbe">DPMA</span><span class="baustein_weight">kurier</span> only informs you
        when there is something to report. What is new is that all those who opt for option two will receive
        filtered messages. Your emails are now reduced to positive messages of the type "There are
        news/changes". Another new feature is that only technical changes are relevant for the restricted
        dispatch option. An update of the XML data record for <span class="baustein_farbe">DPMA</span><span class="baustein_weight">connect</span> users is considered a technical change and is now only
        taken into account for full dispatch. To change the dispatch option, please log in to your personal
        area and open the account settings via the login menu. In the
        <span class="baustein_farbe">DPMA</span><span class="baustein_weight">kurier</span> section, you
        will find the option "I only want to be informed about those of my monitoring activities for which
        there is news". To be informed as much as possible, deselect this option.
    </p>
    <hr>

    <h3 class="card-title dpma-card-min"><a href="https://register.dpma.de/DPMAregister/service/aktuelles#a74">Convenient entry of Nice classes</a>
    <span class="dpma-datum"> (18.07.2025)</span></h3>
    <!-- <h2 class="dpma-h_link" id="a74">Convenient entry of Nice classes<span class="dpma-datum"> (18.07.2025)</span></h2> -->
    <p class="mehrzeilig-ellipsis">
        There is a new selection aid in the basic search for trade marks and in the mask for defining a courier monitoring for trade marks according to Nice classes. If you click on the "Select classes"
        button, a drop-down menu opens with multi-line entries from the group titles of the classes. A search field is used to filter the menu contents. As soon as you click on a menu entry, the class
        number is added to the input field. With a preceding space if there are already numbers in the input field. You can still enter a class number in the "Class(es)" field without using the input help.
    </p>
    <hr>

